WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.053
Welcome to Module 3: Design Qualification,
or DQ.

2
00:00:04.173 --> 00:00:10.040
Our fictional vessel V-201 prepares an
aqueous oral solution before filling.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.272
It is not an aseptic process.

4
00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:16.872
The diagram connects intended purpose to a
proposed design and then to

5
00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:18.379
a reasoned decision.

6
00:00:18.499 --> 00:00:21.848
We ask whether the design can support the
intended use.

7
00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:25.979
A purchase order or attractive equipment
drawing cannot answer that

8
00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:27.592
question by itself.

9
00:00:28.212 --> 00:00:30.879
DQ evaluates the proposed design.

10
00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:34.668
Installation qualification examines what
was installed.

11
00:00:34.788 --> 00:00:39.247
Operational qualification challenges
operation, and performance

12
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:42.865
qualification addresses performance for
the intended use

13
00:00:42.985 --> 00:00:44.756
under defined conditions.

14
00:00:44.876 --> 00:00:48.311
These questions are connected but not
interchangeable.

15
00:00:48.431 --> 00:00:52.975
A successful design review does not
demonstrate that the installed vessel

16
00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:55.271
mixes a real batch uniformly.

17
00:00:55.391 --> 00:00:58.441
Later modules examine those later stages.

18
00:00:58.561 --> 00:01:02.083
Keep the evidence and the decision
appropriate to the stage.

19
00:01:02.703 --> 00:01:07.055
Look at three design concerns: the product
contact path, the measurement

20
00:01:07.175 --> 00:01:08.988
chain and access for cleaning.

21
00:01:09.108 --> 00:01:13.289
A vessel can have a suitable steel body
yet an unsuitable gasket.

22
00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.872
A temperature display can work while
representing the wrong sensor location.

23
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:20.915
A shiny exterior can conceal a trapped
pocket.

24
00:01:21.035 --> 00:01:25.963
For each concern, ask which design feature
addresses the need, what evidence

25
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:29.219
supports that claim and what must later be
verified.

26
00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:34.575
In this course, every equipment
identifier, specification and evidence

27
00:01:34.695 --> 00:01:36.850
reference is a teaching invention.

28
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.466
No site equipment has been qualified.

29
00:01:39.586 --> 00:01:44.663
At the end of a DQ review, state the
design scope, the evidence examined and

30
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:46.276
the open conditions.

31
00:01:46.396 --> 00:01:50.684
Do not write ready for routine production
when only design evidence

32
00:01:50.804 --> 00:01:52.170
has been assessed.

33
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:56.492
Your first activity is to distinguish a
design conclusion from an

34
00:01:56.612 --> 00:01:59.535
installation finding and a performance
claim.
